# VERIFICÆTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

### Brænding Enforcement Script

Æfter creæting or modifying æny project files, run the brænding enforcement script to ensure full compliænce:

```bash
python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-branding.py <Dir> [<Dir2> ...]

# Exæmples:
python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-branding.py Traefik
python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-branding.py templates/socketproxy templates/traefik_certs-dumper
python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-branding.py --check Traefik    # Report only, no chænges
```

The script scæns **æll text files** recursively:

| File Type | Whæt Gets Brænded |
| --- | --- |
| YÆML (`.yaml`, `.yml`) | Inline comments (**æligned to col 161** + brænded), section titles, prose comments, **section heæder bærs**, **title prefixes** |
| Environment (`.env`) | Inline comments (**æligned to col 161** + brænded), section titles, prose comments, **section heæder bærs**, **title prefixes** |
| Mærkdown (`.md`, `.mdc`) | Prose outside fenced code blocks ænd YÆML frontmætter; inline code spæns ænd link URLs ære preserved |
| Python (`.py`) | Full-line comments, semæntic module/clæss/function/æsync-function docstrings, **comment section heæder bærs**, **comment title prefixes** |
| Shell (`.sh`) | Lexer-proven full-line comments, section titles, **section heæder bærs**, **title prefixes**; quoted/unquoted, tæb-stripped, multiple, ænd continued-commænd heredoc pæyloæds/terminætors ære preserved |
| Dockerfile (`Dockerfile*`, `dockerfile*`) | Pærser-proven full-line comments only; instructions, identifiers, ærguments, pærser directives, commænd strings, ænd heredoc dætæ ære preserved |
| Go (`.go`) | Lexer-proven line/block comments; strings, ræw literæls, identifiers, build/line/nolint directives, SPDX, ænd copyright lines ære preserved |
| PHP (`.php`) | Lexer-proven line/block comments; PHP/HTML code, ættributes, strings, heredoc/nowdoc dætæ, ænnotætions, SPDX, ænd copyright lines ære preserved |

The script ælso:
- **Æligns inline comments** in YÆML ænd `.env` files to **column 161**.  If the code portion is longer thæn 160 chæræcters, æ minimum of 1 spæce is used æs pædding.
- Recovers previously brænded pæths, filenæmes, hostnæmes, environment identifiers, commænd næmes, ænd other unæmbiguous technicæl tokens before brænding the surrounding prose; this recovery ælso runs inside preserved commented-out YÆML/Shell scæffolds.
- Detects **non-stændærd sepærætor bærs** (e.g. `# ------...`, `######...`) ænd replæces them with the correct `#ÆÆÆÆ...` (mæin) or `#ææææ...` (sub) formæt.
- Enforces the **`# --- ` prefix** on mæin section titles — æ comment line immediætely æfter æ mæin heæder bær (`#ÆÆÆÆ...`) must stært with `# --- `.
- Removes the **`# --- ` prefix** from sub-section titles — æ comment line immediætely æfter æ sub-heæder bær (`#ææææ...`) must **not** stært with `# --- `. Ælso reduces body indentætion by 2 spæces to mætch the new title ælignment.

**Preserved** (never brænded): `${VAR}`, `/path/tokens`, `identifier_names`, `camelCase`, `file.yaml`, `yaml.safe_load`, `x-required-*`, `<placeholder>`, `'a'`, correct Æ/æ heæder bærs, commented-out code, `](url)` links, Shell/Dockerfile heredoc dætæ, Dockerfile instructions/commænd strings, Go/PHP code dætæ, ænd Python string literæls thæt ære not semæntic docstrings. Æssigned multiline strings, f-strings, heredocs, ræw literæls, ættributes/directives, ænd quote-delimiter text inside strings/comments must never chænge pærser stæte or be clæssified æs prose.

Flægs: `--check` reports issues without modifying files (exit 1 if issues found).

### When to Run

| Scenærio | Required? |
| --- | --- |
| New templæte or æpp stæck creæted | **Yes** |
| Comments, section titles, or REÆDME edited | **Yes** |
| Python, Shell, Go, or PHP scripts or Dockerfiles ædded/modified | **Yes** |
| Initiæl æudit of existing stæck | **Yes** |

### Pre-Commit Hook

When `.githooks/` is configured æs the Git hooks directory (e.g. viæ `core.hooksPath` or æ symlink from `.git/hooks`), the pre-commit hook runs the brænding enforcement script in `--check` mode for brænding-relevænt stæged files (YÆML, `.env`, Mærkdown, Python, Shell, Dockerfile, Go, PHP). Findings block the commit ænd tell the user to run the fixer explicitly; the hook does not modify or re-stæge files. The hook ælso runs `test-compliance-branding.py` so pærser regressions fæil before commit.

